zerosdr (0.3.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add a dismissible first-run guide: H/Tab/Enter overview, observer
    position with inline latitude/longitude entry, and a "show on next
    start" checkbox; reopen it from H -> settings -> SHOW GUIDE
  * Use a GPS position when available (gpsd on 127.0.0.1:2947 or NMEA on
    /dev/serial0, ttyAMA0, ttyS0, ttyUSB0, ttyACM0) and remember it
  * A manually entered position overrides GPS until it is cleared; the
    ADSB settings overlay shows the active source

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:20:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Bundle a readsb build with the RTL-SDR backend at /usr/lib/zerosdr/readsb
    (the Debian readsb package is built without it), prefer it over
    /usr/bin/readsb, and log clearly when no decoder is available
  * Let dh_shlibdeps compute Depends so the bundled decoder's libraries
    (libusb, librtlsdr, ncurses, zstd, zlib) are pulled in automatically

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:40:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * ADSB: translucent radar sweep with a gradient tail, per-revolution
    sonar ping, 90-degree ticks and a new-aircraft chime
  * ADSB: Enter cycles list -> detail -> radar -> list; Left/Right page
    the aircraft list (the Cardputer has no PgUp/PgDn)
  * ADSB: H overlay with the key list and observer position settings
  * ADSB: compact ICAO/ALT/DIST list, selected callsign on a full-width
    strip at the bottom of the panel, anti-aliased TrueType text
  * Link FreeType for the callsign and ADSB status/detail text
  * Fix the debian package architecture note and dependency list

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 15:20:00 +0800

zerosdr (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add on-screen help overlay (H) with a settings tab: FM de-emphasis,
    audio AGC, FFT size and sample rate, persisted in
    ~/.config/zerosdr/sdr_settings.json
  * Rework the Cardputer Zero TCA8418 keymap (F/Z/X/C arrows, Shift for
    coarse tuning, fn layer codes, sym-layer decimal point)
  * Keep the display span inside the captured band when the sample rate
    changes and cycle Y only through usable spans
  * Default FM de-emphasis to 50 us (CN/EU/Asia)
  * Rewrite the README with step-by-step Cardputer Zero deployment and
    add a Simplified Chinese translation
  * Fix the Debian package architecture (arm64)

 -- Weiming Feng <bestedwin@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:10:00 +0800

